<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Perusing assorted Social Media Disgrace fo=
r some Monday inspiration, Football Daily was struck by the amount of scorn=
 and ridicule heaped upon a large group of men dressed in black, many of th=
em wearing balaclavas to hide their identities. Formed with the intention o=
f creating something resembling a matchday atmosphere in and around the Emi=
rates Stadium, the Ashburton Army is a group of wannabe ultras who would al=
most certainly retreat at the speed of light if confronted by one of the mo=
re hardcore continental firms they style themselves after. While many fello=
w fans view them with utter disdain for their =E2=80=9Ctry-hard=E2=80=9D ae=
sthetic, on the same day a large group of identically attired and significa=
ntly older men were marching on Portsmouth to intimidate a boat-load of asy=
lum seekers, the feeling persists that on this occasion, those pouring deri=
sion on this gang of overenthusiastic Ruperts might have set their sights e=
lsewhere.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Widely billed as The Basque 44-Year-Olds W=
ho Grew Up Together In The Antiguo Locale of San Sebasti=C3=A1n and Remain =
Close Friends To This Day derby, there was atmos aplenty at the Emirates St=
adium as Arsenal hosted one of very few teams given a snowball=E2=80=99s ch=
ance in hell of challenging them for the title this season. And while Xabi =
Alonso=E2=80=99s Chelsea took a very early lead courtesy of some uncharacte=
ristically shonky Arsenal defending at a set-piece, <a href=3D"https://abli=
nk.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszc=
CSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgYah5jsyKKBNhx6-BYFiHJAC5PU03gRXQyg-grglRit_akUQ=
Hf1W6_aKcLkE8fRfXmX5eEnEzKKu0u9zGXp4JfFVPKiYQEoR3pNdfoBKlVoyeOk1tTGvHLr8c25=
3Kf-TpXJRyGgowxKQjUYB62df3HtKl2xBihgvM5PQoCZ8q4AbajVX1A0bV55pVnsA-ORNlCHaWW=
L1trtBIramKdmKK_Dt6tfekMmqI-jnGrBdcIJY/4tu/zuSGXgvCSGuc3ud_pNwGuA/h29/h001.=
XvRlPVyV4JK0NfVy6Gq9VeNm2TrhY46aGMFx4163Oko" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">the =
champions ultimately prevailed</a>. Their victory was due in no small part =
to Martin =C3=98degaard, who put in the kind of purring performance we simp=
ly did not often see from the frequently absent or knack-plagued Norwegian =
as his teammates ground out victory after victory en route to last season=
=E2=80=99s title. =E2=80=9CI think he is enjoying his football,=E2=80=9D wh=
ooped Mikel Arteta as he praised his captain after the game. =E2=80=9CHis p=
ersonal life is settled. He is available. He is training. He has his routin=
e and if he is intelligent, he can take a lot of benefits from the players =
around him. I think he was outstanding today.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Having watched Arsenal play three, win thr=
ee and score all six of their goals from open play in the Premier League so=
 far, cynics who spent large tracts of last season criticising Arteta=E2=80=
=99s side=E2=80=99s over-reliance on set-piece goals have had to find new n=
its to pick. No stranger to controversy last season, on Sunday Gabriel Maga=
lh=C3=A3es prompted a nationwide chorus of grumbles for escaping a red card=
 despite kicking the Chelsea goalkeeper in the head. =E2=80=9CMart=C3=ADnez=
 has got the ball in his hands and he boots him in the head,=E2=80=9D obser=
ved Wayne Rooney with a chuckle on Match of the Day. =E2=80=9CI think he=E2=
=80=99s extremely lucky to stay on the pitch.=E2=80=9D And while Football D=
aily is largely against heads being kicked on the football pitch or elsewhe=
re, the decision not to dismiss Arsenal=E2=80=99s defender was correct beca=
use there was no malice aforethought as the Brazilian scrapped for the ball=
 and he did not throw his boot with excessive force. In so many ways this i=
s an Arsenal we are not used to seeing, but one that already looks far bett=
er than the one that won the league.</p>
